A||||6||rodmcneill||Salvage yard motor mileage?||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-21-2001||03:42 PM||||If I buy a used 3.4 Camaro motor from a salvage yard, do I just take their word for the mileage on the motor? If the donor vehicle has been crushed and I cannot check the odometer do they have to keep some kind of records on this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||01-21-2001||05:54 PM||||If you cannot see the vehicle than you are going to have to take their word for it. None of the 4  3.4-liter engines I looked at seemed to have the mileage they claimed they did, which were all supposed to be below 60k miles. When I pulled the heads off two of them they had rust in the cylinders and more wear than I have seen in motors with 200,000 miles. I decided in the end to buy a core and rebuild it myself.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-21-2001||06:31 PM||||im with formula on this one. If you cant see the engine in the car, pass on it. Make sure they dont pull a switch on you too when you pick it up, some yards have no morals. If you can, mark the engine you want somehow, or even get the sn# before you leave. Also if you can be picky, try not to get an engine that has been in a hard frontal crash, chk for broken blocks at mounts, accessories like A/C breaking head at mounting point. Make sure they know that you want the whole thing, theyll strip stuff like starter, compressor if they can, rip and cut wiring harnessess, exhaust manifolds.<P>better yet, see if theyll let you pull it yourself, then youll know you got what you pay for.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-21-2001||08:58 PM||||As USUAL...  great advice guy's!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||6
Z||000004||theogre||01-21-2001||11:52 PM||||I won't buy any motor I can't see running first.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||01-22-2001||11:16 PM||||I agree with THEOGRE!<BR>If I can't hear it and see it run, it's just a rebuildable core! I also like to see the car that the engine came out of, just a bit of insite of the proper care issue!||||reg||6
Z||000006||007DOUG||01-23-2001||12:54 AM||||Late model engines usually come from wrecked cars. Insurance claim would show mileage.<P>Late model cars find their way to your local salavge yard via an auction. The auction house should have the mileage info.<P>Don't know how you'd track down either of the above for info.<P>But i still wouldn't buy without hearing it run.||||reg||1
